<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
        <artifactId>qits-workspaces</artifactId>
        <version>2026.905.164818</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <!-- The git SUBSTRATE: a local mirror per repository, the worktrees the release flow merges in,
         and the pushes that are now the only way a ref moves. Nothing about releases, versions,
         workspaces or rows is here — those stay in `domain`, which calls this through a handful of
         records and two declared ports.

         WHY IT IS ITS OWN MODULE. This service used to reach into the bare origins qits-artifacts
         serves, on a shared volume, and write refs there directly. That is what made branch
         creations, merges and skeleton commits fire no post-receive and produce no CI run. Removing
         it means every one of those becomes a push — and a push needs somewhere to push FROM, which
         is the mirror. Kept behind its own module boundary so the same machinery can later move out
         of this deployable entirely (a mirror daemon, or in-process JGit inside qits-artifacts)
         without the release flow noticing: the seam is the API in this package, not a call graph.

         FRAMEWORK-FREE, deliberately, in the shape of `workspace-daemon-protocol`: no Quarkus, no
         CDI, no MicroProfile config, no jackson. It takes its collaborators as constructor
         arguments, so its tests run offline against throwaway local bares with no container, no
         database and no augmentation — which is the repo's "a clone of this repo alone builds and
         tests green" rule holding one module deeper. `domain` owns the one CDI producer that builds
         it from config. -->
    <artifactId>qits-workspaces-gitmirror</artifactId>
    <name>qits-workspaces :: gitmirror</name>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
